{title: Hosanna, Loud Hosanna}
{artist: Jeanette Threlfall / Ellacombe (1784)}
{genre: Hymn, Children}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: hosanna-loud-hosanna.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Hosanna_Loud_Hosanna-Ellacombe) and the Cyber Hymnal score (96% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Ho[A]san[G#7]na, [E]loud ho[F#m]san[E]na,
[A]The [D]little [Bm]child[E]ren [A]sang;
[A]Through pil[G#7]lared [E]court and [F#m]tem[E]ple
[A]The [D]love[F#m]ly [E]anthem [A]rang.
[A]To Jesus, who [D]had [E]blessed them
[A]Close folded to [D]His [E]breast,
[E]The [A]child[G#7]ren [E]sang their [F#m]prais[E]es,
[A]The [D]simp[F#m]lest [E]and the [A]best.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]From [A]O[G#7]li[E]vet they [F#m]fol[E]lowed
[A]Mid [D]an ex[Bm]ul[E]tant [A]crowd,
[A]The vic[G#7]tor [E]palm branch [F#m]wa[E]ving,
[A]And [D]chant[F#m]ing [E]clear and [A]loud.
[A]The Lord of men [D]and [E]angels
[A]Rode on in low[D]ly [E]state,
[E]Nor [A]scorned [G#7]that [E]little [F#m]child[E]ren
[A]Should [D]on [F#m]His [E]bidding [A]wait.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]Ho[A]san[G#7]na [E]in the [F#m]high[E]est!
[A]That [D]ancient [Bm]song [E]we [A]sing,
[A]For Christ [G#7]is [E]our Re[F#m]dee[E]mer,
[A]The [D]Lord [F#m]of [E]Heaven our [A]king.
[A]O may we ev[D]er [E]praise Him
[A]With heart and life [D]and [E]voice,
[E]And [A]in [G#7]His [E]blissful [F#m]pre[E]sence
[A]E[D]ter[F#m]nal[E]ly re[A]joice!
{end_of_verse}
